# LLHB runner: per-run CLI sandbox HOME (never versioned)
benchmarks/llhb/results/runs/.sandbox/
# What a run leaves behind is versioned by whether it can be regenerated, not
# by what it contains — lovverk is public NLOD 2.0 material, so "no legal text"
# read literally would deny the corpus repo's existence. The rule that holds:
#
#   * regenerable from the corpus pin -> not stored. A tool payload is exactly
#     that: the freeze pins lovverk, so (tool, arguments, pin) reproduces the
#     bytes, and records.jsonl keeps each payload's SHA-256 to check them
#     against. A copy in git would be a duplicate with no evidentiary value.
#   * not regenerable -> stored. Model output is non-deterministic, so an
#     answer nobody kept is an answer nobody can ever re-score. records.jsonl
#     holds every final answer and the full tool trace by name, arguments and
#     payload hash; statutory quotes inside those answers stay, because
#     redacting them would remove the citation fidelity LLHB exists to measure.
#
# raw/ is excluded because a treatment transcript embeds the payloads inline,
# which would put regenerable corpus material back in the repo. What it holds
# beyond records.jsonl — thinking blocks, event order, stderr — is not scored.
benchmarks/llhb/results/runs/*/tools/
benchmarks/llhb/results/runs/*/raw/
